<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kawo Tona Gaga</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tona</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kawo Tona Gaga was the last independent king of Wolaita in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>. When Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a> invaded with a large army in 1894, he led fierce resistance but was wounded and captured. Wolaita was annexed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a>, with tens of thousands killed or enslaved, and Tona is remembered as a hero of Wolaita resistance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kawo-tona-gaga.jpg" alt="Kawo Tona Gaga" width="320" height="418" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown but obviously died 70 years ago · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kawa_Tona.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
